# ESP: PARTLABEL declared once in mkosi.repart/10-esp.conf; fixed mount
# point is the Path= prerequisite of /usr/lib/sysupdate.d/80-uki.transfer.
PARTLABEL=ESP /efi vfat umask=0077,noatime 0 0
# /var (@data): PARTLABEL=var hand-written (consistent with other entries),
# deliberately not using repart auto-generated fs UUID — two-stage build
# (pass1 tar solidifies / pass2 final disk mkfs) produces independent fstab
# state; mismatched values cause fsck to wait for device. Growfs is triggered
# by this entry's x-systemd.growfs; partition-level growth is handled by
# initrd 92-var-grow.conf.
PARTLABEL=var /var btrfs subvol=@data,compress=zstd:1,noatime,x-systemd.growfs 0 0
# @landscape: application payload subvolume (landscape-webserver + static/
# + factory-default toml), decoupled from root OTA for independent update
# via basalt-landscape-update.service. Mount point directory lives inside
# @data, auto-created by systemd mount unit on missing (mount.c mkdir_p_label).
PARTLABEL=var /var/lib/basalt/landscape btrfs subvol=@landscape,compress=zstd:1,noatime 0 0
# Pool top level (subvolid=5, canonical — more stable than name/path): landing
# zone for sysupdate btrfs subvolume create. Without this mount sysupdate
# creates inside the caller process root (running deployment) → nested
# subvolume accidents (UKI top-level addressing broken / vacuum collateral
# deletion / nested blocks removal while update itself "succeeds" silently).
# Mount must be rw: btrfs subvolume create on ro mount returns EROFS directly
# (elemental-operator #923 empiric). This mount is a plain data-volume view
# of @data sibling (pool view shows all subvolumes), no extra protection;
# old deployment ro protection lives at btrfs property layer
# (deployments-readonly.service).
PARTLABEL=var /var/lib/basalt/pool btrfs subvolid=5,noatime 0 0
# No / entry: sysroot.mount is generated by initrd fstab-generator from cmdline
# root= + rootflags=subvol=root-basalt-<N> (rw, full-root writable); systemd-
# remount-fs does nothing for roots without a / entry. Device identity
# (machine-id/ssh keys/network snippets) lives in /var/lib/basalt/state
# (@data plain directory), no separate fstab entry.